.TH rsoftflowd 8  "rsoftflowd 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
rsoftflowd \- Traffic flow monitoring daemon rewritten in Rust
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrsoftflowd\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interface\fR] [\fB\-r\fR|\fB\-\-read\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-pidfile\fR] [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-control\-socket\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-max\-flows\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-\-foreground\fR] [\fB\-D\fR|\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-netflow\-version\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-netflow\-dest\fR] [\fB\-L\fR|\fB\-\-hoplimit\fR] [\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-\-track\fR] [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-export\-protocol\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-sampling\-rate\fR] [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-snaplen\fR] [\fB\-S\fR|\fB\-\-send\-interface\fR] [\fB\-e\fR|\fB\-\-exporter\-ip\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-full\-transport\-header\-check\fR] [\fB\-F\fR|\fB\-\-flow\-lookup\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-load\-balance\fR] [\fB\-6\fR|\fB\-\-track\-ipv6\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-direction\-mac\fR] [\fB\-A\fR|\fB\-\-absolute\-time\fR] [\fB\-B\fR|\fB\-\-pcap\-buffer\-size\fR] [\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-bidirectional\fR] [\fB\-R\fR|\fB\-\-psamp\-port\fR] [\fB\-M\fR|\fB\-\-multithread\fR] [\fB\-N\fR|\fB\-\-no\-promisc\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-mpls\-labels\fR] [\fB\-I\fR|\fB\-\-reinit\-interval\fR] [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-gauge\-cpu\-clock\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-\-adjust\-time\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIbpf_program\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
rsoftflowd is a software implementation of a flow\-based network traffic monitor.
It reads network traffic and gathers information about active traffic flows. 
A \*(Aqtraffic flow\*(Aq is communication between two IP addresses or (if the 
overlying protocol is TCP or UDP) address/port tuples.
